<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  STEREO_INTERCEPT world (Phase-2 T16, ADR-0046 F1 DECIDED: "trajectory-
  matched offline-render REPLAY" -- the ground stereo rig's frames are
  rendered OFFLINE by teleporting the target along its deterministic dash
  path (scripts/rig_snapshot_capture.py); the REAL detect+triangulate+track
  pipeline (T18/T19) replays those frames LIVE at flight time, paced by sim
  time, over the real :47800 link. Live rig rendering during an actual
  flight is DEFERRED behind a pre-registered probe gate (ADR-0046 item 4),
  not built here -- a live 3rd/4th camera at design resolution collapses
  Gazebo's real-time factor the same way worlds/apriltag_demo.sdf's single
  extra 1280x720 camera did (RTF ~0.05), confirmed rig-specific by
  scripts/probe_stereo_rtf.sh. Council: 3/3, no dissent on the pick; see
  docs/decisions.md ADR-0046 for the full record.)

  BYTE-IDENTICAL to worlds/markerless.sdf (physics / scene / ground_plane /
  sun / spherical_coordinates kept EXACTLY -- PX4's gz_bridge depends on it,
  docs/goals.md M2) EXCEPT for two deliberate changes:

    1. World name is "stereo_intercept" (not "markerless"). Every gz-
       transport topic for this run keys off it, e.g.
       /world/stereo_intercept/model/x500_mono_cam_0/link/camera_link/sensor/imager/image
       and /world/stereo_intercept/set_pose. The flight stack already reads
       the world name from the INTERCEPTOR_WORLD_NAME env var
       (scripts/m2_detect.py's WORLD_NAME, reused by m3/m4/mover/
       s2_cue_mock/rig_snapshot_capture.py), so set
       INTERCEPTOR_WORLD_NAME=stereo_intercept to match this file.

    2. ADDED: an <include> of model://ground_stereo_rig (models/
       ground_stereo_rig/, T16) at the `broadside_160m` pose from
       docs/rig_geometry_analysis.md Sec 2 / logs/rig_geometry/coverage.csv
       -- the recommended PRACTICAL (off-flight-line) pose: rig center at
       world (-153.5, 0.0, 1.8) [1.8 m tripod-class mount height per
       docs/stereo_design.md's mount], yaw 0 rad, so its boresight (link
       local +X) points back along world +X at the fixed-X=6.5 m dash
       corridor -- a 160.0 m standoff (6.5 - (-153.5) = 160.0), the rig's
       own design-envelope ceiling (docs/stereo_design.md).

       WEDGE-COVERAGE SANITY CHECK (recomputed here, cross-checked against
       coverage.csv's 91%/91% figure): each camera's half-angle is
       0.349 rad / 2 = 0.1745 rad (10 deg). At the corridor's row
       (x=6.5, ~160 m downrange of the rig), the shared wedge's half-width
       is 160 m * tan(10 deg) = ~28.2 m, i.e. it covers target world-Y in
       roughly [-28.2, +28.2]. The dash profile (scripts/m4_target_mover.py,
       scripts/rig_geometry_analysis.py) sweeps Y from +-29.3 m through
       Y=0 -- so the wedge covers the corridor for ALL of the dash except
       the first ~1.1 m of travel from the +-29.3 m start (the single most
       oblique, farthest moment of CUE_WAIT: |y|=29.3 gives an off-boresight
       angle of atan(29.3/160)=10.36 deg, just outside the 10 deg
       half-angle) -- through HANDOFF (~160.8 m range -> ~10 m range) and
       on to the y=+-5 m boundary scripts/rig_snapshot_capture.py samples
       to. This matches coverage.csv's `broadside_160m` row: 0.914 path
       fraction covered, both directions (r2l/l2r), continuous from just
       after CUE_WAIT start through HANDOFF. The counter-intuitive reason
       this pose (not a closer one) wins: at fixed half-angle, absolute
       wedge width GROWS with standoff (docs/rig_geometry_analysis.md
       Sec 2), so the farther-back, design-envelope-ceiling pose covers
       more of the corridor than any closer candidate tested.

       The target <include> (fpv_target_markerless) is UNCHANGED from
       markerless.sdf: same model, same pose (5, 0, 0.5), same identity
       orientation -- the flight stack still moves it via set_pose during
       ENGAGE/the rig capture harness. Set
       INTERCEPTOR_TARGET_MODEL=fpv_target_markerless (the default) to
       match.

  Launch (mirrors worlds/markerless.sdf): reachable as
  ${PX4_GZ_WORLDS}/stereo_intercept.sdf at runtime (symlink like
  markerless.sdf -- scripts/check_t16.sh creates/repairs it, ADR-0005
  pattern), models via GZ_SIM_RESOURCE_PATH:

    PX4_GZ_WORLD=stereo_intercept \
    GZ_SIM_RESOURCE_PATH=~/interceptor-sim/models \
    HEADLESS=1 make px4_sitl gz_x500_mono_cam

  With INTERCEPTOR_WORLD_NAME=stereo_intercept
  INTERCEPTOR_TARGET_MODEL=fpv_target_markerless set for any flight-stack
  script (m2/m3/m4_*.py, scripts/rig_snapshot_capture.py) run against this
  world.
-->
<sdf version="1.9">
  <world name="stereo_intercept">
    <physics type="ode">
      <max_step_size>0.004</max_step_size>
      <real_time_factor>1.0</real_time_factor>
      <real_time_update_rate>250</real_time_update_rate>
    </physics>
    <gravity>0 0 -9.8</gravity>
    <magnetic_field>6e-06 2.3e-05 -4.2e-05</magnetic_field>
    <atmosphere type="adiabatic"/>
    <scene>
      <grid>false</grid>
      <ambient>0.4 0.4 0.4 1</ambient>
      <background>0.7 0.7 0.7 1</background>
      <shadows>true</shadows>
    </scene>
    <model name="ground_plane">
      <static>true</static>
      <link name="link">
        <collision name="collision">
          <geometry>
            <plane>
              <normal>0 0 1</normal>
              <size>1 1</size>
            </plane>
          </geometry>
          <surface>
            <friction>
              <ode/>
            </friction>
            <bounce/>
            <contact/>
          </surface>
        </collision>
        <visual name="visual">
          <geometry>
            <plane>
              <normal>0 0 1</normal>
              <size>500 500</size>
            </plane>
          </geometry>
          <material>
            <ambient>0.8 0.8 0.8 1</ambient>
            <diffuse>0.8 0.8 0.8 1</diffuse>
            <specular>0.8 0.8 0.8 1</specular>
          </material>
        </visual>
        <pose>0 0 0 0 -0 0</pose>
        <inertial>
          <pose>0 0 0 0 -0 0</pose>
          <mass>1</mass>
          <inertia>
            <ixx>1</ixx>
            <ixy>0</ixy>
            <ixz>0</ixz>
            <iyy>1</iyy>
            <iyz>0</iyz>
            <izz>1</izz>
          </inertia>
        </inertial>
        <enable_wind>false</enable_wind>
      </link>
      <pose>0 0 0 0 -0 0</pose>
      <self_collide>false</self_collide>
    </model>
    <light name="sunUTC" type="directional">
      <pose>0 0 500 0 -0 0</pose>
      <cast_shadows>true</cast_shadows>
      <intensity>1</intensity>
      <direction>0.001 0.625 -0.78</direction>
      <diffuse>0.904 0.904 0.904 1</diffuse>
      <specular>0.271 0.271 0.271 1</specular>
      <attenuation>
        <range>2000</range>
        <linear>0</linear>
        <constant>1</constant>
        <quadratic>0</quadratic>
      </attenuation>
      <spot>
        <inner_angle>0</inner_angle>
        <outer_angle>0</outer_angle>
        <falloff>0</falloff>
      </spot>
    </light>
    <spherical_coordinates>
      <surface_model>EARTH_WGS84</surface_model>
      <world_frame_orientation>ENU</world_frame_orientation>
      <latitude_deg>47.397971057728974</latitude_deg>
      <longitude_deg> 8.546163739800146</longitude_deg>
      <elevation>0</elevation>
    </spherical_coordinates>

    <!-- Markerless target: tag-less enemy quad body at (5, 0, 0.5), approach
         face (-X) toward the interceptor at origin (see
         models/fpv_target_markerless/model.sdf for the facing derivation --
         same convention as apriltag_target). NO fiducial: the seeker must lock
         the body. UNCHANGED from worlds/markerless.sdf. -->
    <include>
      <uri>model://fpv_target_markerless</uri>
      <name>fpv_target_markerless</name>
      <pose>5 0 0.5 0 0 0</pose>
    </include>

    <!-- T16 ground stereo rig (ADR-0046 F1): `broadside_160m` pose from
         docs/rig_geometry_analysis.md Sec 2 / logs/rig_geometry/coverage.csv
         -- world (-153.5, 0.0, 1.8), yaw 0 rad, boresight along +X, 160 m
         standoff, facing the fixed-X=6.5 m dash corridor. See the world
         header comment above for the wedge-coverage sanity check
         (~28.2 m half-width at the corridor's row -- 91%/91% path coverage
         both dash directions, per coverage.csv). -->
    <include>
      <uri>model://ground_stereo_rig</uri>
      <name>ground_stereo_rig</name>
      <pose>-153.5 0.0 1.8 0 0 0</pose>
    </include>
  </world>
</sdf>
